.TH CTRL-EXEC-API 8 "2026-06-10" "ctrl-exec" "ctrl-exec Manual"
.SH NAME
ctrl-exec-api \- HTTP API server for ctrl-exec
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctrl-exec-api
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctrl-exec-api
exposes the ctrl-exec run, ping, discovery, and status operations over HTTP
on the control host. It reads its configuration from
.B ctrl-exec.conf
and uses the same auth hook as the CLI. By default it binds to
.I 127.0.0.1
on port 7445; set
.B api_bind
and
.B api_port
in the configuration to change this. The hook is read at startup, so
restart the service after changing it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Path to
.BR ctrl-exec.conf .
Default:
.IR /etc/ctrl-exec/ctrl-exec.conf .
.SH CONFIGURATION
Relevant keys in
.BR ctrl-exec.conf :
.TP
.B api_port
Port to listen on (default 7445).
.TP
.B api_bind
Bind address (default 127.0.0.1).
.TP
.B api_cert ", " api_key
TLS certificate and key (plain HTTP if absent).
.TP
.B auth_hook
Auth hook executable.
.TP
.B auth_deny_generic
When set, denied requests return a generic 403 without the specific reason.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ctrl-exec-dispatcher (8),
.BR ctrl-exec-agent (8).
.PP
Full HTTP API reference: the API document shipped with ctrl-exec and
.UR https://github.com/OpenDigitalCC/ctrl-exec
.UE .
